(PRC-11 — all three directory statements set the error flag on failure
 and `On error` catches it; the program keeps running.
 The create failure is a path under /proc, which no unprivileged process
 may write to; the other two name a directory that does not exist.
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-11.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   create set the error flag
   remove set the error flag
   delete set the error flag
   change directory set the error flag
   execution continued past all four
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control".
Create a directory called "/proc/not_allowed".
On error print "create set the error flag".
Remove the directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_absent".
On error print "remove set the error flag".
Delete the directory "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_absent".
On error print "delete set the error flag".
Change directory to "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_absent".
On error print "change directory set the error flag".
print "execution continued past all four".
